h0"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\n\nMax Weber famously wrote that politics is \"a strong and slow boring of hard boards.\" In [Why it took 4 years to get a lock files specification](https://snarky.ca/why-it-took-4-years-to-get-a-lock-files-specification/), Brett Cannon demonstrates how the same principle applies to technical coordination in open source.\n\nPython recently adopted [PEP 751](https://peps.python.org/pep-0751/) for lockfile specification. Doing so","key":"vZQVRqspQW"}],"key":"AmprUKoiQR"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"S2IB0ufpai"}],"key":"IboK9EzvLC"},{"type":"text","value":"October 21, 2025 | ","key":"yM1rzBXKtJ"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"rzNUX6FQoh"}],"key":"fxIOx7Rurk"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"c8tBrsan9I"}],"key":"O8eyxKxjvS"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2025/lock-files","dataUrl":"/blog.2025.lock-files.json","internal":true,"protocol":"file","key":"hyWX2RIks7"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2025/jet-lag","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"My system for beating jet lag","key":"GVsfLbpmrJ"}],"key":"JZSKVF76WD"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\nI travel internationally a lot, which means I deal with a lot of jet lag. This post is a quick summary of a system I've found helpful, based on [this paper](https://www.frontiersin.org/articles/10.3389/fphys.2019.00927/full).\n\n\nThe basic idea is to shift your body's internal clock by timing your exposure to light, exercise, and melatonin around","key":"RC3SHXLcZp"}],"key":"mu4HKpQHqW"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"VPQePtmTaK"}],"key":"EOLHiBXS5L"},{"type":"text","value":"October 18, 2025 | ","key":"miqhClyTRJ"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"Q4ThRr2ws6"}],"key":"NjmYGLS6J5"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"hWZR6x2vNG"}],"key":"Xu2aFBhOOV"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2025/jet-lag","dataUrl":"/blog.2025.jet-lag.json","internal":true,"protocol":"file","key":"T0rkXuoItF"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2025/fund-systems-not-developmend","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Why open source foundations try to fund systems, not development","key":"PuxpAhqaVM"}],"key":"DOvqIOPOxf"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\nThis is a brief reflection on something that I've been hearing consistently from the Linux Foundation and its member projects as part of serving on the [Board of the Jupyter Foundation](https://jupyterfoundation.org). Here's a point that originally surprised me when I heard it:\n\n> Most foundations within the Linux Foundation network recommend","key":"VtBxmZINqC"}],"key":"gTppKyeEiZ"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"NcwYZ04BFz"}],"key":"MMgf75fasP"},{"type":"text","value":"May 31, 2025 | ","key":"WMlnSdFaMG"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"tnlieyeyhN"}],"key":"djfhcSlnyy"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"tb9Se0rVZ2"}],"key":"RmdndqBwjd"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2025/fund-systems-not-developmend","dataUrl":"/blog.2025.fund-systems-not-developmend.json","internal":true,"protocol":"file","key":"E8GNE7Nioj"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2025/more-contributors","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Jupyter can align the needs of its community and its foundation by enabling contribution","key":"dp7kCO1k8z"}],"key":"zryOY6zAbP"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\nThis week was my first time attending the [Linux Foundation Member Summit](https://events.linuxfoundation.org/lf-member-summit/). This is an annual meeting for all of the Linux Foundation member organizations and projects. I joined because of my new role [on the Jupyter Executive Council](./jec.md), and so I tried to go into this meeting with the","key":"cghYARvpou"}],"key":"IXDN0XGpaJ"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"wbvsUqrqoF"}],"key":"IXfa6NDqqD"},{"type":"text","value":"March 22, 2025 | ","key":"M2cOEksnx9"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"odhRHXWGnH"}],"key":"LldBG3mY0L"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"VK1EzDsbh4"}],"key":"cdga7YH9xO"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2025/more-contributors","dataUrl":"/blog.2025.more-contributors.json","internal":true,"protocol":"file","key":"Qw7LTVsH6Q"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2025/jupyter-org-structure","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The relationship between the Jupyter Executive Council, Software Steering Council, and Foundation","key":"gVOMcsdWvl"}],"key":"L7isbKChgH"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\n\nThis is a question that I've been asked many times now that I'm serving on the ","key":"YL41RzaCES"},{"type":"abbreviation","title":"Jupyter Executive Council","children":[{"type":"text","value":"JEC","key":"erAAkIx9Si"}],"key":"ZW6cVQImSO"},{"type":"text","value":" and the ","key":"y5iAWdjE4U"},{"type":"abbreviation","title":"The Jupyter Foundation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"JF","key":"n7v8nVMGfu"}],"key":"jBRQT89nFN"},{"type":"text","value":". I'm writing up a quick response so that I have something to refer back to and align my own thinking on.\n\n**How most Linux Foundation projects seem to be structured**. Linux","key":"vKgp5CJnEm"}],"key":"D7vRqJggeE"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"tKyNiGz24z"}],"key":"dj1Aj6FOzX"},{"type":"text","value":"March 02, 2025 | ","key":"tlVK0oF8Im"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"E70GzGs46Q"}],"key":"igDiap4D7q"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"f9yBjsYt2b"}],"key":"UOZxPGQbAD"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2025/jupyter-org-structure","dataUrl":"/blog.2025.jupyter-org-structure.json","internal":true,"protocol":"file","key":"CCUBKZrANa"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2025/os-support","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ways the Jupyter Foundation could support open source projects","key":"TIpW8buBX0"}],"key":"YSaXV3O5E9"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\nThe Jupyter Foundation has a pot of money and it aims to use that funding quickly to support the Jupyter Project. But what should it use the funding _for_? There are many things to do, and not enough time or money to try everything. This is a brief brainstorm and","key":"XlWex0OpzB"}],"key":"wN1yCMktGf"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"UEJs9wF1VE"}],"key":"ETtIFeIsg6"},{"type":"text","value":"February 26, 2025 | ","key":"vuAtpwLH67"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"zIGH3jy4Yz"}],"key":"Qm10GwV0CE"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"R59N3CRkza"}],"key":"NcARZFieCC"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2025/os-support","dataUrl":"/blog.2025.os-support.json","internal":true,"protocol":"file","key":"tOV7g98oxZ"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2025/jec","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Why I'm running for the Jupyter Executive Council","key":"n7ephPmBu0"}],"key":"k5jWXIA5B5"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\n\nThis year, I decided to nominate myself for the [Jupyter Executive Council](https://jupyter.org/governance/executive_council.html). This is a brief post explaining my rationale for doing so, the kind of service I'd hope to provide the project, and where I imagine the project moving.\n\n\nThe [Jupyter Executive Council](https://jupyter.org/governance/executive_council.html) is the highest governing body within the","key":"nDNYegRfDL"}],"key":"BFCuhWztnt"},{"type":"f